          "source": null,
          "kind": "scalar",
          "choices": null
        },
        {
          "name": "t",
          "unit": "m",
          "desc": "thread thickness at the root (square p/2; 29\u00b0 Acme \u2248 0.63p \u2014 not the 0.37p flat width)",
          "lo": null,
          "hi": null,
          "label": null,
          "integer": false,
          "signed": false,
          "source": null,
          "kind": "scalar",
          "choices": null
        }
      ],
      "equations": [
        "sigma_B = 2*F/(pi*d_m*n_t*p)",
        "c_arm = (d_m - d_r)/2",
        "sigma_b = 6*F*c_arm/(pi*d_r*n_t*t**2)"
      ],
      "procedure": null,
      "outputs": [
        "sigma_B",
        "c_arm",
        "sigma_b"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Bearing stress uses the projected pitch-line area \u03c0\u00b7d_m\u00b7(p/2) per engaged thread, so \u03c3_B = 2F/(\u03c0\u00b7d_m\u00b7n_t\u00b7p). Bending models each thread as a cantilever of depth c_arm = (d_m \u2212 d_r)/2 and root section \u03c0\u00b7d_r\u00b7t carrying F/n_t at the pitch line (\u03c3_b = M\u00b7(t/2)/I with M = (F/n_t)\u00b7c_arm and I = \u03c0\u00b7d_r\u00b7t\u00b3/12). Threads are assumed to share the load equally \u2014 real nut threads load unevenly (first engaged thread \u2248 0.38F).",
        "For a square thread (depth p/2, so c_arm = p/4 and t = p/2) this reduces exactly to the standard \u03c3_b = 6F/(\u03c0\u00b7d_r\u00b7n_t\u00b7p). The root thickness t is a geometry input (square: p/2; 29\u00b0 Acme \u2248 p/2 + 2\u00b7(0.25p)\u00b7tan14.5\u00b0 \u2248 0.63p), not a built-in table. [Reviewer fix 2026-09-15: Acme guidance previously quoted the 0.37p flat width; example geometry made a consistent square thread.]"
      ],
      "method_references": [
        "\u03c3_B = 2F/(\u03c0\u00b7d_m\u00b7n_t\u00b7p); cantilever thread-bending model (Shigley sec. 8-2 form, recalled)"
      ],
